### Frontpage API — manual requests
# JetBrains IDEs: click ▶ next to a request and pick an environment (local / railway).
# VS Code: install the "REST Client" extension, then "Send Request".
# Environments live in http-client.env.json (committed, no secrets).
# Put tokens in http-client.private.env.json (git-ignored).
# Start the backend first: `bun run dev:backend` from the repo root.

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health
Accept: application/json

### CORS — allowed origin (expect Access-Control-Allow-Origin in the response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### CORS — disallowed origin (expect no Access-Control-Allow-Origin)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/health
Origin: https://evil.example

### Unknown route → JSON 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/does-not-exist

### Malformed JSON body → JSON 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/health
Content-Type: application/json

{ not json

### Fetch a feed (RSS 2.0) → normalized JSON
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/fetch?url=https://css-tricks.com/feed/
Accept: application/json

### Fetch an Atom feed
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/fetch?url=https://vercel.com/atom
Accept: application/json

### Conditional fetch → 304 when the feed is unchanged (paste the ETag from the previous response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/fetch?url=https://vercel.com/atom
If-None-Match: "paste-etag-here"

### Dead feed → 502 { error: { code: "http_4xx", retryable: false } }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/fetch?url=https://example.com/this-feed-does-not-exist.xml

### Not a feed → 422 { error: { code: "not_a_feed" } }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/fetch?url=https://example.com/

### Missing url → 400 { error: { code: "invalid_url" } }
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/fetch

### Auth — sign up (email + password; sets the session cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-up/email
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: http://localhost:3000

{ "email": "ada@example.com", "password": "correct horse battery", "name": "Ada" }

### Auth — sign in
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: http://localhost:3000

{ "email": "ada@example.com", "password": "correct horse battery" }

### Auth — current session (null when signed out; 503 without a database)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/get-session

### Auth — request a password reset (without RESEND_API_KEY the email goes to Mailpit, http://localhost:8025, or the backend log)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/request-password-reset
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: http://localhost:3000

{ "email": "ada@example.com", "redirectTo": "http://localhost:3000/reset-password" }

### Auth — reset password with the token from the reset link (the part after /reset-password/)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/reset-password
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: http://localhost:3000

{ "token": "paste-token-here", "newPassword": "staple battery horse" }

### Auth — untrusted return address → 403 { code: "INVALID_REDIRECT_URL" }
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/request-password-reset
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: http://localhost:3000

{ "email": "ada@example.com", "redirectTo": "https://evil.example/reset-password" }

### Auth — send an email-verification code (sign-up sends one too; read it in Mailpit)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/email-otp/send-verification-otp
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: http://localhost:3000

{ "email": "ada@example.com", "type": "email-verification" }

### Auth — verify the email with the code (signs the user in; errors: INVALID_OTP, OTP_EXPIRED, TOO_MANY_ATTEMPTS)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/email-otp/verify-email
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: http://localhost:3000

{ "email": "ada@example.com", "otp": "123456" }

### Auth — change password (signed in; wrong current password → INVALID_PASSWORD)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/change-password
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: http://localhost:3000

{ "currentPassword": "correct horse battery", "newPassword": "staple battery horse", "revokeOtherSessions": true }

### Auth — sign out
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sign-out
Origin: http://localhost:3000

### Subscriptions — list mine, with each feed's health (sign in first; signed out → 401 unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions

### Subscriptions — subscribe by URL → 201 { subscription } + Location (the feed is fetched and checked first)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "url": "https://css-tricks.com/feed/" }

### Subscriptions — subscribe into one of my categories (someone else's or a missing one → 404 category_not_found)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "url": "https://vercel.com/atom", "categoryId": "paste-category-id-here" }

### Subscriptions — the same feed again → 409 { error: { code: "already_subscribed", subscriptionId } }
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "url": "https://css-tricks.com/feed/" }

### Subscriptions — not a feed → 422 { error: { code: "not_a_feed" } }
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "url": "https://example.com/" }

### Subscriptions — rename (trimmed; over 200 characters → 400 bad_request)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/paste-subscription-id-here
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customTitle": "My CSS reading" }

### Subscriptions — clear the custom title (the feed's own title shows again)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/paste-subscription-id-here
Content-Type: application/json

{ "customTitle": null }

### Subscriptions — move to Uncategorized
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/paste-subscription-id-here
Content-Type: application/json

{ "categoryId": null }

### Subscriptions — unsubscribe → 204 (bookmarks stay; someone else's or a missing id → 404 not_found)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/paste-subscription-id-here

### Items — the first page of everything I follow, newest first (sign in first; signed out → 401 unauthorized)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items

### Items — the next page: paste the previous page's nextCursor (null means there are no more)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items?cursor=paste-next-cursor-here

### Items — one category, unread only (someone else's or a missing category → 404 category_not_found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items?category=paste-category-id-here&unread=true

### Items — Uncategorized, oldest first, 10 per page
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items?category=uncategorized&order=oldest&limit=10

### Items — one feed: its feedId from GET /api/subscriptions (a feed I don't follow → 404 feed_not_found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items?feed=paste-feed-id-here

### Items — feed and category together → 400 bad_request
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items?feed=paste-feed-id-here&category=uncategorized

### Items — a limit over 100 → 400 bad_request
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items?limit=101

### Items — counts per feed, per category and in total, for the sidebar
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items/counts

### Items — one article with its full content (doesn't mark it read; a feed I don't follow → 404 not_found)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/items/paste-item-id-here

### Items — mark read (isRead: false marks unread); up to 100 ids, ids outside my feeds are skipped → { updated, counts } (counts: just the touched feeds)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/items/read
Content-Type: application/json

{ "itemIds": ["paste-item-id-here"], "isRead": true }

### Items — mark all as read: everything, until the first page's asOf (newer items stay unread) → { asOf, undo, counts } (counts: the scoped feeds)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/items/mark-all-read
Content-Type: application/json

{ "asOf": "paste-asOf-from-GET-api-items" }

### Items — mark all as read: one category ("uncategorized" too), or send { "feed": "…" } for one feed
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/items/mark-all-read
Content-Type: application/json

{ "category": "uncategorized" }

### Items — undo a mark-all: paste its `undo` object unchanged → { counts } (counts: the touched feeds)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/items/mark-all-read/undo
Content-Type: application/json

{ "asOf": "paste-undo-asOf", "cutoffs": [], "marks": [] }
